-- DICT-SEMANTICS §4 `gen-rec` with the context INFERRED rather than ascribed --
-- the `gen` sourcing (`P'` read off the body) instead of the `gen-sig` sourcing.
-- s4-gen-rec-shared-dict-params is the ascribed twin; this is the rule's other
-- antecedent, and the two are DIFFERENT code paths per #610's mechanism note
-- (declared context vs body-occurrence-derived context).
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived):
--   SCHEMES: evenSz : Sz a => a -> Int -> Bool
--            oddSz  : Sz a => a -> Int -> Bool
--   VALUES:  `sz w` is 1 at `w = (1 : Int)`, so both arms decrement by one:
--            evenSz 6 -> oddSz 5 -> ... -> evenSz 0 = True      => True
--            oddSz  7 -> evenSz 6 -> ... -> evenSz 0 = True     => True
--
-- OBSERVED: check ACCEPT with exactly those two schemes; run/build print
-- True then True. CONFORMANT.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS ROW DOES **NOT** DISCRIMINATE GROUP SOURCING FROM PER-BINDING SOURCING,
-- and an earlier revision wrongly claimed it did ("both bindings, not just the one
-- whose body mentions `sz` first"). BOTH bodies here dispatch on `Sz`, so
-- per-binding inference and §4's group-wide `P'` produce the identical answer --
-- the fixture cannot tell them apart, and the claim was inert. The claim has been
-- deleted rather than weakened.
--
-- 🔬 The DISCRIMINATING form -- a group where only ONE body dispatches, so the
-- other can acquire `Sz a =>` only from the group -- lives in its own fixture,
-- `s4-gen-rec-inferred-asymmetric.mdk`, because it does not currently execute:
-- `check` accepts and reports both schemes, and BOTH engines then refuse to run
-- it. What remains pinned here is the ordinary symmetric case as a regression
-- guard on the schemes and the values.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz Int where
  sz n = n

evenSz w n = if n == 0 then True else oddSz w (n - sz w)

oddSz w n = if n == 0 then False else evenSz w (n - sz w)

main =
  println (evenSz (1 : Int) 6)
  println (oddSz (1 : Int) 7)
